{%- doc -%}
  Materia Themes. A sample garment for the Boutique Rail section: a real photo
  of a garment, cut out, shown until a garment has its own pictures (when the
  section's Show sample garments is on). Your own pictures always replace it.

  @param {number} [index] - Which sample (0-7); defaults to kind
  @param {number} [kind] - Kept for older calls: used as the index when index is not given
  @param {string} view - 'side' (on the rail) or 'front' (on hover and in focus)
  @param {string} [sizes] - The sizes attribute for the picture

  @example
  {% render 'boutique-rail-sample', index: 0, view: 'front' %}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Photo credits (Storelib, round 26: streetwear samples). Real photographs of
  garments on their hangers, from Unsplash (Unsplash License), cut out by
  machine and cleaned by hand; the hook above each is drawn by the section,
  so the photographs' own hooks are trimmed off.
  1 Charcoal hoodie, 3 Oat hoodie, 5 Forest hoodie, 7 Grey hoodie
      - https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1620799140188-3b2a02fd9a77, the white hoodie tinted
  2 White boxy tee  - https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1778671394516-8270eac13c42
  4 Black long sleeve, 6 Black boxy tee
      - https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1610502778270-c5c6f4c7d575
  8 Black crew      - https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1618354691551-44de113f0164
  The side views are drawn from each garment's own front photograph (strips of
  it resampled into a garment hanging side on); they are not photographs taken
  from the side. License: https://unsplash.com/license
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign n = index | default: kind | default: 0 | modulo: 8 | plus: 1
  if view == 'side'
    assign w = 336
    assign cls = 'brail__side'
  else
    assign w = 688
    assign cls = 'brail__front'
  endif
  assign file = 'brail-sample-' | append: n | append: '-' | append: view | append: '.webp'
-%}
<img class="{{ cls }} brail__photo" src="{{ file | asset_url }}" width="{{ w }}" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"{% if sizes %} sizes="{{ sizes }}"{% endif %}>
